From fe2447e35002bfaf42cce61761986d737123b989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:44:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 113/149] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2: Hold
 the panels in reset from boot

The boot loader leaves both panels running from a command-mode pipeline
with autorefresh. Linux has no hand-over for it: the display clock
controller's probe stops it early in the boot, in the middle of a frame,
and the panels then show their corrupted frame memory (DSC slices of
coloured noise) for several seconds, until the panel driver resets them
at the first modeset. systemd-boot has cleared the screen by then, so
there is no picture to keep.

Drive both reset lines low (asserted) from the pin controller's probe,
before any display driver: the panels stay dark until the panel driver
brings them up. The state only configures the pins and claims no
function, so the panels' own pin states still apply, and the panel
driver takes the lines as they are.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2.dts | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2.dts
index a87f8c9f0c6e..27af2a53ecc0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2.dts
@@ -1279,6 +1279,24 @@ earpiece: speaker@0,3 {
 &tlmm {
 	gpio-reserved-ranges = <4 4>, <12 4>, <56 4>, <76 4>;
 
+	/*
+	 * Both panels are held in reset from here on, until the panel driver
+	 * brings them up. The boot loader leaves a command-mode pipeline
+	 * running (autorefresh) that Linux cannot take over: the display
+	 * clock controller's probe stops it in the middle of a frame, and the
+	 * panels then show corrupted frame memory (coloured noise) for
+	 * seconds, until their first modeset. In reset they stay dark.
+	 * Configuration only, no function: the panels' own states still
+	 * claim the pins.
+	 */
+	pinctrl-0 = <&disp_reset_hold>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+	disp_reset_hold: disp-reset-hold-state {
+		pins = "gpio50", "gpio51";
+		output-low;
+	};
+
 	/* The camera sensors' XCLR lines (the vendor DT's active states) */
 	cam_tele_reset_default: cam-tele-reset-default-state {
 		pins = "gpio17";
